# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Kazuma Ito et al. (2024). Machine learning interatomic potential with DFT accuracy for general grain boundaries in α-Fe.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-024-01451-y
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 63e2268845ca3be9...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 149 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the level-22 MTP for alpha-Fe, its VASP reference
# calculations, the two-part training set (domain-expertise and RANDSPG
# structures), and the energy and force RMSEs the text states for the
# training and validation sets and for cells cut from nano-polycrystals
# (general grain boundaries and triple junctions).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
